WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.002 --> 00:00:00.835
- Hi, everyone.

00:00:00.835 --> 00:00:03.010
I'm Claire, I'm a Tasty
producer, and today,

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:04.880
I'm gonna show you some
back to school recipes

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.480
that you can make for your kids.

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:14.157
Meal prepping is something
that I like to do

00:00:14.157 --> 00:00:16.090
on a weekly basis.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:18.820
It helps me stay organized
and makes me feel

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:21.170
like I have a little
bit of my life together.

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:23.210
I've found that I actually
eat so much healthier

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.550
when I plan out for the whole week.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:29.540
So, transitioning that same
concept into meals for children

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:32.460
is such a great idea, and
as a parent, it saves time.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.040
One of the easier ways to
plan meal prepping for kids

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:38.120
is to pick a base
vegetable, a base protein,

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.520
and a base fruit to put in every lunch.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:43.690
You can mix it up day to day
by having one or two choices.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:46.510
So, in this video, what
my coworker Hannah did

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:49.410
was she picked a couple of base vegetables

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:52.100
and a couple base fruits to play with

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.870
so that way she can
add one or the other in

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:57.270
for a little variation and
to keep lunch interesting.

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:58.880
When I first started making lunches

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:00.580
for my niece and my nephew,

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.050
the video I turned to was this one.

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:06.090
It's really fun to give kids
variety with their lunches.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:10.250
I think that making lunch
an activity helps with that,

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:12.980
and having build your own kind of dishes

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:14.680
makes it really exciting to eat

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:16.520
and lets them be a little
creative with their lunch.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:17.890
I know how difficult it is

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:19.610
to make a different lunch every day,

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:21.210
and when that lunchbox comes home

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:24.030
and all of that food
is just still in there,

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:25.440
it drives me nuts.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.960
So, I try to make things as
exciting as I possibly can.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:29.150
I'm all about convenience,

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:31.240
and just to make it even more convenient,

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:34.470
you can utilize the same
ingredients in different forms

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:37.320
so that way you're not
having to spend extra money

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:40.380
buying extra ingredients to
make four days worth of food.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:42.690
You could just buy one
package of tortillas

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:44.410
and make three different things out of it.

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:45.850
I think packing lunches is important

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:49.440
because it's one way that I
can show my niece and nephew

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:50.590
that I care about them,

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:52.284
and I ask for their feedback all the time.

00:01:52.284 --> 00:01:53.310
Did you like this?

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:54.190
Did you like that?

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:56.170
Can I put this in your lunch tomorrow too?

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:59.200
And if I get an excited yes,
I know I've done a good job.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.111
By no means do you have to follow

00:02:01.111 --> 00:02:04.070
exactly what is in the video to a tee.

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:06.270
You can customize it to make

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.420
whatever you think your child would like.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.290
Obviously, not every kid is gonna like

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.570
hard boiled eggs in their
lunch, but that's okay.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:13.680
You can put in something else

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:14.870
that you do know that they like,

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:16.560
that way you can provide them with a lunch

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:18.170
that you know they're gonna enjoy,

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:20.450
but is also gonna give
them sustainable energy

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:22.000
throughout the rest of the day.

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:26.510
Another way you can meal prep
is by using leftover chicken,

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:28.430
or you can buy one chicken, shred it up,

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:29.720
and make your lunches from there.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:32.385
Chicken is one of the most
popular meats in the world,

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:34.900
and just about every kid
I know will eat chicken.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:37.840
There's a variety of recipes
that you can make with chicken,

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.310
which is why it's perfect

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:41.113
for meal prepping for kid's lunches.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.830
Like I said before, you can use
these as jumping off points.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.830
If your kid doesn't like chicken salad,

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:47.900
you can make your own version

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.565
or mix it up with your
favorite family recipe.

00:02:49.565 --> 00:02:50.908
This is just another way

00:02:50.908 --> 00:02:53.890
to optimize your
efficiency in the mornings.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:55.650
You just have one solid protein

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:56.990
and you expand on it from there,

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.640
and you can really go anywhere with it.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.990
Just make sure to remove
all the bones and cartilage

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:02.510
and shred the chicken really well.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:05.450
Growing up in my house,
I hated eating leftovers.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:08.800
So, my mom would get sneaky and
she would turn the leftovers

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.770
into something new so I wouldn't even know

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:12.455
that I was eating leftovers for lunch.

00:03:12.455 --> 00:03:14.750
So, that was something
that really inspired me

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:17.728
to make this video and to
pay homage to my childhood

00:03:17.728 --> 00:03:19.323
as well as my upbringing.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.590
If it wasn't leftovers,

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:23.020
my lunches were typically pretty boring

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:24.390
and the same every day.

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:26.950
So, I didn't want the same
for my niece and nephew,

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:29.310
and that's why I put in a lot of effort

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.943
to make their food
exciting and fun to eat.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:33.460
My niece is only six,

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:36.780
so having a full day at
school is a really long time

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:40.230
for her to go without having
a snack every five minutes.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:42.920
I really like making sure
that she has healthy choices

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:44.120
for her lunch every day.

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:45.900
Making a lunch that she brings home

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:49.230
with the box totally empty
is such a satisfying feeling.

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:50.350
When you're that age,

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:52.630
lunch is such an exiting time of the day,

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:54.950
and it's even an exciting
time of the day for me

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:56.243
as a 25-year-old woman.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:57.942
One of my favorite things to do

00:03:57.942 --> 00:04:01.250
that my mom used to do
for me is to leave notes

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:03.580
in their lunches with
funny little sayings,

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:07.070
and I absolutely think
that I'm the funniest aunt

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:08.530
in the whole entire world

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:11.780
because I leave the
cheesiest, corniest notes,

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:14.643
and I crack myself up as I'm
writing them every morning.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:17.610
I like to add puns on little
notes in their lunches,

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:20.993
and I think I'm funny, but I
don't know if anyone else does.

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:23.883
But come on, I be-leaf in you.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:25.903
Come on.

00:04:25.903 --> 00:04:28.143
Lettuce taco 'bout it.

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:30.453
You've bean a good kid today.

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:31.443
I'm funny.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:33.703
Give me the credit, I'm funny.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:37.710
For my nephew, since he's only
three, he can't really read,

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.560
but my niece is starting
to be able to read

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:42.480
and she either gets my
jokes or kinda looks at me

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:45.510
in disappointment like oh,
auntie, that was a drab one.

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:46.960
I always thought it was so special

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:48.880
when my mom would put notes in my lunch

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:51.330
because it was just a little
reminder from her to me

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:53.170
that she loves me and cares about me,

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:56.120
so I'm carrying on that tradition
with my niece and nephew.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:03.330
These cereal bars are the
best snack for any time.

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:05.750
You can grab 'em and go for the morning,

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:06.940
you can put 'em in a lunch,

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:08.590
you can have 'em as an after school snack.

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:10.640
They really are the perfect
food for any time of day.

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:11.510
When you're making these,

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:14.280
it's a perfect opportunity
to involve your child

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.640
in the cooking process with you.

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:18.230
It's the best when you see how
proud they are of themselves

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:19.960
and you see a big smile across their face.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:22.700
My coworker Hannah's son,
Jackson, helped me make this,

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:25.640
and he's usually my sous
chef in Tasty Junior videos.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:26.710
This particular day,

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:28.350
he was really upset that we were putting

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:29.940
the yogurt chips in the mix.

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:31.920
I had to tell him they're
part of the recipe

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:33.870
and we have to put them in,
but you know what we can do?

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:36.230
We can make a batch
separately just for you

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:37.650
that doesn't have yogurt chips in it,

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:40.963
and he really enjoyed having
his own little version.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:43.450
At the time, I was a
little frustrated with him

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:45.750
because he was changing my vision,

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:47.900
but he really taught me a valuable lesson

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:50.640
in that you should always
customize your recipes

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:51.820
to your own preference.

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:53.040
Another reason these are great

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:56.300
is because you can wrap them
up and save 'em in your fridge

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.930
for about three months before
you'll need to toss them.

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:02.010
These are just another way for
you to save time, and also,

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:04.800
this way you know what
ingredients are going in

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:07.410
compared to the mystery
ingredient sugar filled bars

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:08.960
that there are out there today.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:10.300
Now, with this snack,

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.370
I can't tell you exactly
what they're based on,

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:15.810
but it starts with cheese
and it's a great snack,

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:18.740
but we'll just call them
baked cheese crackers for now.

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:20.310
My favorite part about this recipe

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:22.200
is that it's four ingredients.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:24.000
It really doesn't take that long to make,

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.690
just a little bit of effort,
but the effort is worth it.

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:28.980
These are something that I
make for myself all the time,

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:31.510
and they pair really well
with chardonnay, by the way.

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:33.550
They're lighter and they have

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:36.190
a really satisfying crunch to them.

00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:39.000
Have the kids help you cut out the shapes

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.510
and put them on a baking sheet

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:41.680
and poke a hole in the middle.

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:42.920
When you use the cookie cutters,

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:46.290
it just makes it so much more
fun and so much more kid-like.

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:47.900
You can add these into lunches,

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:50.060
you can keep them for an at-home snack,

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:52.506
you can hide them in the back
of the pantry for yourself.

00:06:52.506 --> 00:06:54.640
Whatever you do, just make them.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:56.850
You can even play with the type of cheese

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:57.760
that you put in them.

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:01.023
You can do mozzarella,
Colby jack, American.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:02.673
No, don't do American.

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:04.930
Mozzarella, Colby jack, pepper jack

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:08.420
if you're a little fancy, or
you can even amp up the flavor

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:10.360
with a really great sharp cheddar

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:14.113
and you'll have really
flavorful and delicious cracker.

00:07:14.510 --> 00:07:16.730
You can also use a cookie cutter

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:18.770
and just keep rolling out the dough

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:20.623
until you don't have any dough left.

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:21.760
Just like last time,

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:24.440
I told you guys that I do read
the comments, and believe me,

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:26.230
I know you can buy these in a box,

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:28.100
but making them is so much better

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:30.800
and you can make the cutest little shapes,

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:33.973
and they taste 10 times better, promise.

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:35.043
Go make them.

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:37.430
I mean, it's only four ingredients

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:39.080
you probably have in your house right now.

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:41.960
It's another surefire way
of making sure you know what

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:44.710
your kids are eating and
what's going into those foods.

00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:52.150
This is another four
ingredient really easy snack.

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:54.320
You could even really do
it with three ingredients.

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:55.980
You're really just dehydrating the fruit,

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:57.438
and that's what's taking so long,

00:07:57.438 --> 00:07:59.450
but the end result is worth it.

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:01.560
If you were to compare these to rolls

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:03.280
that you would buy at the store,

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:05.080
you could look and see that there's far

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.830
less processed ingredients.

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:09.450
These are something that
you can do in big batches.

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:11.700
You can do two or three
sheet pans at a time

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:13.870
since they do take so long to bake.

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:15.510
These are really really fun to eat,

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:17.400
and it's along the same lines of using

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:19.719
little to no added sugar.

00:08:19.719 --> 00:08:23.090
Just peel right off of the
parchment paper that they're on,

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:25.340
and I would even eat them
as a snack for myself

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:27.140
because they're just that delicious.

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:28.810
The last school year
was a really interesting

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:30.130
learning process for me.

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:34.010
I had to relearn what kids
like in their lunches.

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:37.660
My now six-year-old niece
and three-year-old nephew

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:40.773
landed in my life just like a bomb.

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:44.420
I don't have the typical aunt,
niece, nephew relationship.

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:46.440
My mom and I are their caregivers,

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:49.250
and it's been a really
big learning experience

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:53.100
for me to make them lunches
and play this role for them

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:55.030
that was so different from anything

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:56.670
I'd ever done in my life before that.

00:08:56.670 --> 00:08:59.100
It's really taken a lot of self-reflection

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.790
and looking back on my
childhood and my life

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:03.690
to help me learn what to feed them,

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:07.170
and it's a lot of testing,
asking for their feedback,

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:08.850
but they always have so much gratitude

00:09:08.850 --> 00:09:10.280
for the food that we make them,

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:13.043
and I am so lucky to have
such wonderful kids to feed.

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:15.280
Before they came into our care,

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:17.870
I was barely making lunch for myself,

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:20.080
let alone eating something other than

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:21.560
pizza rolls from the freezer.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:24.460
So, it's been a big
opportunity for me to explore

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:26.860
some of my favorite dishes
from when I was a kid

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:29.560
and bring them back to share
with my niece and nephew.

00:09:29.570 --> 00:09:30.660
School's already hard enough,

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:32.770
and kids really look forward
to their lunch breaks.

00:09:32.770 --> 00:09:34.080
I know I can't be there all the time

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:35.540
while they're at school and I'm at work,

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:37.620
but knowing that I've
provided them with food

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:39.170
that I know they're gonna love,

00:09:39.170 --> 00:09:40.793
it just makes it all worth it.

00:09:42.315 --> 00:09:43.148
That was it.

00:09:44.356 --> 00:09:45.939
- [Andrew] Oh, yes!

00:09:49.652 --> 00:09:51.902
(laughing)

